 "final_message": "I made all twelve changes, and the 6 tests pass (the 4 existing ones plus the 2 new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137. Only a `converted` value of `True` counts as converted.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test for the `None` rule in section 1 and one for keeping the last duplicate id in section 5.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, `conversions_in_window` now says the last `days` entries. I added the `daily_conversion_counts` entry. I also reworded the `dedupe_sessions` entry to say it keeps the last session per id.\n- **Item 12:** Three more functions broke the spec, and I fixed them:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts the keys.\n  - `longest_conversion_streak` now resets the streak at a zero entry. Before, it counted every non-zero entry in the list.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with a `converted` field that isn't `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_session_log` raise a `ValueError` naming the line number. You may want a different behaviour there.",
